ty&rsquo;s 6 grids in Spalding County came in under 90% of normal in October to November in 35 of the 75 years since 1951. In 2025, the middle of the grids ran 46% of normal in September to October and 167% in May to June. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 15782 at 59% that year. A preliminary estimate puts August to September 2026 at 77.7 on grid 16083.</p>"}
